<div class="section">
  <p>The Chromaverse was, undeniably, a perplexing place.  It wasn’t a world of solid matter, of predictable landscapes or recognizable forms. Instead, it was a vast, shimmering expanse of pure color and shifting geometry, a canvas of impossible angles and impossible textures.  And within this chaotic beauty lived Horace, a hedgehog with spectacles perched precariously on his nose, a solitary observer of a reality utterly devoid of the familiar.</p>
